From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 02:53:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 87/87] web-app: reply icon before the timestamp, real Material
 Symbols glyph

Move the reply-count badge in the message footer from after the
timestamp to before it, and swap the placeholder chat_bubble.svg icon
for Google's Material Symbols "reply" glyph (images/icons/reply.svg),
matching how the project's other Material icons are sourced.

The badge gets a rounded pill background on hover and keyboard focus so
it reads as a button rather than as more metadata. It mixes from
`currentColor`, which is already the metadata text color, so the same
rule covers the light theme, the dark theme and the white-on-media
variant without per-theme overrides.

Bubbles inside the ReplyThread dialog no longer show their own reply
badge: a reply that itself has replies would let you open another
thread dialog on top of the one you're already in, and so on without
end. `Message` gains an optional `inReplyThread` prop, set only by
the dialog.

Bubbles inside the dialog also get "Show in chat" at the top of their
context menu. A bubble in the thread is out of context, and the hover
shortcut's jump button only exists for forwarded/saved copies, so there
was no way back to the message's place in the chat. It reuses the
gallery's jumpToMessage call, which already closes all dialogs; the
same `inReplyThread` prop gates it.

The dialog opens scrolled to the message it was opened from, which
plays the same fade as a jump-to-message highlight in the chat. The
scroll happens once on first load, not on every live refetch, so new
replies don't yank the reader back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
